---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
import { webPage } from '../lib/schema';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — SpeedReflex';
const description = 'How SpeedReflex handles your data: location stays on your device, test history stays in your browser, and there are no accounts.';
const updated = 'September 28, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={webPage({ href: '/privacy/', name: title, description })}>
  <article class="shell max-w-3xl py-16 sm:py-24">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-display-sm sm:text-display">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-mute">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose-sr mt-10">
      <p>
        <span translate="no">{SITE.domain}</span> (“SpeedReflex”, “we”) is built so that we don’t need your personal data. This page explains
        exactly what happens when you use the site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10! text-heading-md text-ink">Location (GPS Speed Tests)</h2>
      <p>
        The online speedometer and the car, bike, bus, train and flight speed tests ask your browser for your location only after you press Start. Positions are processed
        in your browser to calculate speed, distance, altitude and heading. <strong>They are never sent to our servers or to anyone
        else.</strong> When you close the page the trip is gone, unless you choose to export it as a GPX file to your own device.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10! text-heading-md text-ink">Test History and Settings</h2>
      <p>
        Reaction test results, F1 start times, your preferred units (including on the stopping distance calculator), speed-alert settings and theme are saved in your browser’s local
        storage so they’re there next time. This data stays on your device. You can remove test history with the Clear History button,
        or remove everything by clearing this site’s data in your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10! text-heading-md text-ink">Accounts, Cookies and Tracking</h2>
      <p>
        There are no accounts. We don’t set advertising or tracking cookies, and fonts are served from our own domain rather than from a
        third party.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10! text-heading-md text-ink">Server Logs</h2>
      <p>
        Like any website, our hosting provider may keep short-lived technical logs (such as IP address, browser type and the page
        requested) to deliver the site and protect it from abuse. We don’t use them to identify you.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10! text-heading-md text-ink">Sharing Results</h2>
      <p>
        When you share a result or challenge link, the link contains only your score (for example <code>?challenge=231</code>). You choose
        where to send it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10! text-heading-md text-ink">Changes and Contact</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes we’ll update the date above. Questions?
        Email <a href="mailto:privacy@speedreflex.com">privacy@speedreflex.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
